<title>USA: Merrill to buy back up to 750,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Merrill to buy back up to 750,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>ST PAUL, Minn. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Corp said Friday its board of directors has authorized the repurchase of up to 750,000 shares of its 7.9 million common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The purchases will be made from time to time on the open market through brokered transactions, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Merrill provides on-demand 24-hour-a-day typesetting, printing, document reproduction, imaging and distribution services to financial, legal, corporate and commercial markets worldwide.</p>
<p>Shares of Merrill were trading up 1/8 to 21-1/4.</p>
<p>		     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
